Previously, group lookups would occur by an API call that could return a list of groups, filtered by the name and access level. A second lookup would then occur once the group ID was found (to get an object that could actually be used to update the group).

Now, the main path is to do a direct lookup with the group name (e.g. llnl if the repo is at llnl/GRAPE), which is much faster. This path does not handle access level, so the other path is maintained as a fallback.

For an application, the runtime for \"grape approve\" retrieving the top level group dropped from \~5 to \~4 seconds.

This update will likely slightly improve the performance of other commands such as \"grape review\" and \"grape publish\".

